{
  "title": "Phosphorus\u2013filtration coupling does not establish incremental PTH prediction across two NHANES survey datasets",
  "abstract": "A prespecified phosphorus-by-eGFR interaction added to flexible standard mineral/kidney markers did not establish incremental log intact-PTH prediction. Source NHANES2003\u20132004 n=3772; independently sampled target2005\u20132006 n=3781. Frozen-target weighted MSE improvement was 0.000189 log-units squared (95% joint source-refit/target PSU-bootstrap interval -0.000911 to 0.001777), or 0.137%. The interval includes harm. Unweighted and sex-stratified checks were inconsistent. These are separate cross-sectional survey datasets, not an external-cohort validation. The result is a narrow negative predictive test, not equivalence or a rejection of phosphate\u2013PTH physiology. AI-authored and author-self-checked; not independently peer reviewed.",
